{"title":"Career roadmap · Family Business Manager","role":"Family Business Manager","summary":"A Family Business Manager helps operate, grow, professionalise, and eventually transform a family-owned enterprise. The role can cover strategy, finance, sales, operations, people management, digital transformation, governance, succession planning, and new-business development.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Unlike a conventional entry-level job, this career is often built inside the family's existing business. Therefore, practical business responsibility, measurable results, and the ability to professionalise systems are more important than certificates alone."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest career combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA Entrepreneurship/Family Business","Business Operations","Finance","Sales","Digital Transformation","Data Analytics","Governance","Entrepreneurship","Practical Family-Business Experience"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"During UG"},{"text":"Business Intern / Family Business Trainee"},{"text":"Learn the business"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Family Business Executive"},{"text":"Functional responsibility"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Business Operations Associate"},{"text":"Processes and operations"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Business Development Executive"},{"text":"Revenue and expansion"}],[{"text":"2–4 Years"},{"text":"Family Business Manager"},{"text":"Multi-function management"}],[{"text":"3–6 Years"},{"text":"Business Unit Manager"},{"text":"P&L and team responsibility"}],[{"text":"4–8 Years"},{"text":"General Manager"},{"text":"Business performance"}],[{"text":"5–10 Years"},{"text":"Business Head / Operating Partner"},{"text":"Growth and strategy"}],[{"text":"8–15 Years"},{"text":"Managing Director / Executive Director"},{"text":"Enterprise leadership"}],[{"text":"Long Term"},{"text":"Promoter / Owner / CEO"},{"text":"Ownership + strategic leadership"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The title Family Business Manager is not a standardised corporate designation. In practice, responsibilities vary significantly according to the size, structure and maturity of the family enterprise."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BBA","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Understand the Business"},{"type":"p","text":"The first year should focus on learning how a real business works."},{"type":"h","text":"Business fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accounting"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Business mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Marketing"},{"text":"Business law"},{"text":"Organisational behaviour"},{"text":"Entrepreneurship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the family business"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Products/services"},{"text":"Customers"},{"text":"Suppliers"},{"text":"Competitors"},{"text":"Revenue streams"},{"text":"Cost structure"},{"text":"Distribution channels"},{"text":"Key employees"},{"text":"Major business risks"},{"text":"Current technology"},{"text":"Business strengths and weaknesses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Financial basics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Revenue"},{"text":"Gross margin"},{"text":"Operating expenses"},{"text":"EBITDA"},{"text":"Cash flow"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Receivables"},{"text":"Payables"},{"text":"Inventory"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-1 project"},{"type":"h","text":"Family Business Diagnostic Report"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Product","Customer","Revenue","Cost","Profit","Cash Flow","Operations","Competition"]},{"type":"p","text":"Identify the top 10 improvement opportunities."},{"type":"flow","items":["Year 2 — Operations","Finance","Sales"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from observation to actual responsibility."},{"type":"h","text":"Financial management"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial statements"},{"text":"Ratio analysis"},{"text":"Budgeting"},{"text":"Cash-flow management"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Cost control"},{"text":"Pricing"},{"text":"Break-even analysis"},{"text":"Profitability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Working capital"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Inventory + Receivables − Payables = Working Capital Requirement"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how slow collections or excess inventory can create cash-flow problems even when the business is profitable."},{"type":"h","text":"Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Production/service delivery"},{"text":"Quality"},{"text":"Logistics"},{"text":"Vendor management"},{"text":"Process optimisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sales"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lead generation"},{"text":"Customer acquisition"},{"text":"CRM"},{"text":"Sales pipeline"},{"text":"Customer retention"},{"text":"Pricing"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Key-account management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-2 project"},{"type":"h","text":"Family Business Operations Improvement Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one measurable problem:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inventory wastage"},{"text":"Slow collections"},{"text":"Manual billing"},{"text":"Low customer retention"},{"text":"Procurement inefficiency"},{"text":"High operating cost"},{"text":"Poor sales tracking"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Before","Intervention","After"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Digital Transformation + Data"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the next-generation family-business manager can create significant value."},{"type":"h","text":"Business technology"},{"type":"p","text":"